or Germany after winning in 1988 for the German Democratic Republic."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Behind Zeidler, Ntouskos was never a factor, finishing last (sixth) in the final. Van Dorp was second at all the early checkpoints but he struggled in the last 500 metres and had to settle for bronze, having been passed by " [:a {:href "/athletes/153637"} "Yauheni Zalaty"] " (AIN). This was only the second medal for a Netherlands rower, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/39037"} "Jan Wienese"] " won gold in 1968. Zalaty was last through 1,000 metres but had the strongest finish to take the silver medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143464"} "Oliver Zeidler"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/153637"} "Yauheni Zalaty"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AIN.png"}] "AIN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/145589"} "Simon van Dorp"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/141020"} "Tim Brys"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazon